%I A398780 #19 Sep 17 2026 23:58:41
%S A398780 1,1,1,1,2,4,12,57,556,12304,638217,69174215
%N A398780 Number of nonequivalent neighborhood-Sperner graphs on n vertices.
%C A398780 A graph G is neighborhood-Sperner if its family of open neighborhoods {N_G(v) : v in V(G)} is a Sperner family. Two neighborhood-Sperner graphs are considered equivalent if their families of open neighborhoods are isomorphic.
%H A398780 L. H. Clark, S. Holliday, J. P. McSorley and T. D. Porter, <a href="https://opensiuc.lib.siu.edu/math_articles/119/">Enumerating labelled graphs with certain neighborhood properties</a>, Congressus Numerantium 190 (2008), 193-206.
%e A398780 For n=6, there are 13 graph-isomorphism classes of neighborhood-Sperner graphs, but only 12 equivalence classes, since the nonisomorphic graphs C_6 and 2K_3 have isomorphic families of open neighborhoods.
%Y A398780 Cf. A399822 (labeled neighborhood-Sperner graphs), A399817 (labeled neighborhood-Hausdorff graphs).
%K A398780 nonn,more,new
%O A398780 0,5
